WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.750
Claimant: Hi, I’m calling to report that my $850 laptop was stolen from a locked library locker during a 30-minute visit, and it hasn’t been recovered. I filed a police report that afternoon.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.550
Adjuster: Was there any visible damage to the locker or its lock, like pry marks or a broken latch?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.550
Claimant: I don’t know whether there was any visible damage to the locker or its lock.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.200
Adjuster: Understood. Do you know who took the laptop?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.550
Claimant: I don’t know who took it.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:55.650
Adjuster: Decision: requires further review. The claimant reports theft from a locked library locker and a police report, but cannot confirm the visible entry damage required by CA-HO4-THEFT. Forcible entry and applicability of the endorsement’s off-premises exclusion remain unresolved. Next action: Obtain the police report and available locker inspection records or photographs, and review the endorsement’s specific off-premises exclusion before deciding coverage.
